{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-132147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{2}^{2})$ with $P(X>2)=0.3085,$ find $\\mu .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6554\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6915\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =1-P(X>2) \\\\  & =1-0.3085 \\\\  & =0.6915\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =0.6915 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2-\\mu }{2}) & =0.6915 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2-\\mu }{2}) & =0.6915 \\\\ \\frac{2-\\mu }{2} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6915)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.5)=0.6915\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6915)=0.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-\\mu }{2} & =0.5 \\\\ 2-\\mu  & =1 \\\\ \\mu  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-132147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{5}^{2})$ with $P(X\\ge -1)=0.5793,$ find $\\mu .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4207\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4602\\,$ | $\\,0.4562\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5000\\,$ | $\\,0.4960\\,$ | $\\,0.4920\\,$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & =P(X<-1) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\ge -1) \\\\  & =1-0.5793 \\\\  & =0.4207\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & =0.4207 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{-1-\\mu }{5}) & =0.4207 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{-1-\\mu }{5}) & =0.4207 \\\\ \\frac{-1-\\mu }{5} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.4207)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.2)=0.4207\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.4207)=-0.2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1-\\mu }{5} & =-0.2 \\\\ -1-\\mu  & =-1 \\\\ \\mu  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-132145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.25"] ["math" "-0.75"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "0.25"] ["math" "0.75"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-132145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-276190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{6}^{2})$ with $P(X<5)=0.7734,$ find $\\mu .$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ | $\\,0.7454\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ |\n\n$\\mu =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-276190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5)=0.7734\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le 5)=0.7734\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{5-\\mu }{6}) & =0.7734 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{5-\\mu }{6}) & =0.7734 \\\\ \\frac{5-\\mu }{6} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.75)=0.7734\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)=0.75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-\\mu }{6} & =0.75 \\\\ 5-\\mu  & =4.5 \\\\ \\mu  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-276190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-276190" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-276190" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-339311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Suppose that $X∼N(\\mu ,{5.5}^{2})$ and $P(X\\le 18.2)=0.5871.$ Find $\\mu .$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5398\\,$ | $\\,0.5438\\,$ | $\\,0.5478\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6179\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ |\n\n$\\mu =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-339311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 18.2) & =0.5871 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{18.2-\\mu }{5.5}) & =0.5871 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{18.2-\\mu }{5.5}) & =0.5871 \\\\ \\frac{18.2-\\mu }{5.5} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.5871)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.22)=0.5871\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.5871)=0.22.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18.2-\\mu }{5.5} & =0.22 \\\\ 18.2-\\mu  & =1.21 \\\\ \\mu  & =16.99.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-339311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-339311" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-339311" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16.99"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{7}^{2})$ with $P(X<6)=0.6736,$ find $\\mu .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6331\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6700\\,$ | $\\,0.6736\\,$ | $\\,0.6772\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<6)=0.6736\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le 6)=0.6736\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6) & =0.6736 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{6-\\mu }{7}) & =0.6736 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{6-\\mu }{7}) & =0.6736 \\\\ \\frac{6-\\mu }{7} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.45)=0.6736\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)=0.45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-\\mu }{7} & =0.45 \\\\ 6-\\mu  & =3.15 \\\\ \\mu  & =2.85.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-94828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94828" "field" 