the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.60)=0.7257\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7257)=0.60.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & =0.60 \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}={2.5}^{2}=6.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94856" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-94856" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94856" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5.45"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "6.25"] ["math" "6.5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94856" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6.25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(1.5,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X<2)=0.5910,$ use the table value to find ${\\sigma }^{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5478\\,$ | $\\,0.5517\\,$ | $\\,0.5557\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ | $\\,0.5910\\,$ | $\\,0.5948\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ | $\\,0.6293\\,$ | $\\,0.6331\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2)=0.5910\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le 2)=0.5910\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =0.5910 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{2-1.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.5910 \\\\ Φ\\,(\\frac{0.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.5910 \\\\ \\frac{0.5}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.5910)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.23)=0.5910\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.5910)=0.23.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.5}{\\sigma } & =0.23 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{0.5}{0.23} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈2.173\\,91,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}=(2.173\\,91)^{2}≈4.73.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-ca