le 1) & =0.9382 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{1-(-1)}{\\sigma }) & =0.9382 \\\\ Φ\\,(\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.9382 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.9382)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.54)=0.9382\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.9382)=1.54.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =1.54 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{1.54} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈1.30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-341651" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341651" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(3,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X\\ge 1)=0.8413,$ use the table to find $\\sigma .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1841\\,$ | $\\,0.1814\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =P(X<1) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\ge 1) \\\\  & =1-0.8413 \\\\  & =0.1587\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =0.1587 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{1-3}{\\sigma }) & =0.1587 \\\\ Φ\\,(-\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.1587 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.1587)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.00)=0.1587\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.1587)=-1.00.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =-1 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-341655" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341655" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(1.8,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X\\ge 4)=0.2119,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =1-P(X\\ge 4) \\\\  & =1-0.2119 \\\\  & =0.7881\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =0.7881 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{4-1.8}{\\sigma }) & =0.7881 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2.2}{\\sigma }) & =0.7881 \\\\ \\frac{2.2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.80)=0.7881\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)=0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.2}{\\sigma } & =0.80 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2.2}{0.80} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}={2.75}^{2}=7.56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-94857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2.75"] ["math" "3.45"] ["math" "5.63"] ["math" "6.45"] ["math" "7.56"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7.56"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-2<X<2)=0.6578,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8508\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ | $\\,0.8554\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2<X<2) & =0.6578 \\\\ 2P(0<X<2) & =0.6578 \\\\ P(0<X<2) & =0.3289 \\\\ P(X<2)-P(X<0) & =0.3289 \\\\ P(X<2)-0.5 & =0.3289 \\\\ P(X<2) & =0.8289 \\\\ P(X\\le 2) & =0.8289\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =0.8289 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{2-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.8289 \\\\ Φ\\,(\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.8289 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8289)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.95)=0.8289\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.8289)=0.95.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =0.95 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{0.95} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈2.105\\,26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(2.105\\,26)^{2} \\\\  & ≈4.43\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-341991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Aca