\\\\ P(X<3)-P(X<0) & =0.3023 \\\\ P(X<3)-0.5 & =0.3023 \\\\ P(X<3) & =0.8023 \\\\ P(X\\le 3) & =0.8023\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.8023 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.8023 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.8023 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8023)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.85)=0.8023\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.8023)=0.85.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =0.85 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{0.85} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈3.53.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-276229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dddc5a3b492eb5eb76ba9d59ae7c3969142bbe8f43cbe118fc05c50d57b387"} {"question" "q-276229" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-276229" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3.53"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070321/state.json" "file_sha256" "19d4ab8572713c782a9c02de3c79ad3a210fce60d047a06de2fe9aa05767eaac"} {"question" "q-94892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution fu